What is Pandas?
Pandas is a popular Python library used for data analysis and data manipulation.
In simple words:
Pandas helps you work with data stored in tables, similar to Excel spreadsheets, but using Python.

You can use Pandas to:
•	Read data from CSV, Excel, SQL, JSON, etc. 
•	Clean missing or incorrect data 
•	Filter and sort data 
•	Add or remove columns 
•	Calculate statistics 
•	Group and summarize data 
•	Merge different datasets 
•	Prepare data for Machine Learning 
•	Analyze real-world business data


Applications of Pandas
Pandas is mainly used wherever we need to collect, clean, transform, analyze, and understand structured data.

1.  Data Analysis
Pandas is heavily used to analyze business data.

Real-world example:
A company has sales data and wants to know:
•	Total sales 
•	Average sales 
•	Best-selling product 
•	Best-performing city 
•	Monthly revenue


