Type of file in pandas using max.

 CSV (.csv) — most common for tabular data
pd.read_csv("data.csv") 
 Excel (.xlsx) — spreadsheets
pd.read_excel("data.xlsx") 
JSON (.json) — web/API data
pd.read_json("data.json") 
SQL (.db, .sqlite) — database data
pd.read_sql(query, connection)



 
Think of a Pandas table like an Excel sheet:
Name	Age	City
Rahul	20	Delhi
Priya	21	Lucknow
1. Column ↕️
A column goes from top to bottom.
•	Name = one column 
•	Age = one column 
•	City = one column 
2. Row ↔️
A row goes from left to right.
•	Rahul | 20 | Delhi = one row 
•	Priya | 21 | Lucknow = one row 
3. Cell 
A cell is one individual box/value where a row and column meet.
For example:
20 is a cell.
It is at the intersection of the Age column and Rahul's row.
Easy memory 
Column = vertical
Row = horizontal
Cell = one box/value

 
