What is a DataFrame?
The most important concept in Pandas is the DataFrame.
Think of a DataFrame as an Excel spreadsheet inside Python.
For example:
Name	Age	City	Salary
Rahul	25	Delhi	40000
Priya	28	Mumbai	50000
Amit	24	Pune	35000
Ex---
import pandas as pd

data = {
    "Name": ["Rahul", "Priya", "Amit"],
    "Age": [25, 28, 24],
    "City": ["Delhi", "Mumbai", "Pune"],
    "Salary": [40000, 50000, 35000]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

print(df)
Selecting a Row----
Use .iloc.
print(df.iloc[0])

print(df.iloc[1])


Selecting Multiple Rows-----
print(df.iloc[0:2])

Filtering Data----------------
his is one of the most important Pandas concepts.
Suppose the company wants employees whose salary is greater than ₹40,000.

result = df[df["Salary"] > 40000]

print(result)

Basic DataFrame Information----------------
Number of rows and columns

print(df.shape)

Column names—
print(df.columns)

Data types---
print(df.dtypes)

